{number: 54}
{title: We Have Heard the Joyful Sound}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] We have heard the joyful sound: Jesus saves! Jesus saves!
Spread the tidings all a-[G7] round: Jesus saves! [C] Jesus saves!
Bear the [F] news to every [C] land, climb the [F] steeps and cross the [C] waves;
Onward! 'tis our Lord's com-[G7] mand: Jesus [C] saves! [G7] Jesus [C] saves!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Waft it on the rolling tide: Jesus saves! Jesus saves!
Tell to sinners far and [G7] wide: Jesus saves! [C] Jesus saves!
Sing, ye [F] islands of the [C] sea; echo [F] back, ye ocean [C] caves;
Earth shall keep her jubi-[G7] lee: Jesus [C] saves! [G7] Jesus [C] saves!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Sing above the battle strife: Jesus saves! Jesus saves!
By His death and endless [G7] life: Jesus saves! [C] Jesus saves!
Sing it [F] softly through the [C] gloom, when the [F] heart for mercy [C] craves;
Sing in triumph o'er the [G7] tomb: Jesus [C] saves! [G7] Jesus [C] saves!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Give the winds a mighty voice: Jesus saves! Jesus saves!
Let the nations now re-[G7] joice: Jesus saves! [C] Jesus saves!
Shout sal-[F] vation full and [C] free to the [F] utmost of the [C] waves;
This our song of victo-[G7] ry: Jesus [C] saves! [G7] Jesus [C] saves!
{end_of_verse}
